From ac421e8397e6d6de6d5e30297bf8a3bffbc3e47b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <meischris39@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:55:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] EyeToy: add the microphone

The EyeToy's audio interface answered with empty packets, so games that
listen through the camera heard nothing.

Bring in PCSX2's USB microphone device, which its EyeToy embeds for
endpoint 2, and give it an ALSA capture backend in place of cubeb. With
no device named, it takes the microphone on the same USB device as a
V4L2 camera, so a webcam's own mic is used, and otherwise any USB
microphone. Capture is non-blocking and read as the game asks for it,
so no thread is needed; an overrun from a game that stops listening
just restarts the stream.

PCSX2's audio.h carries a Keil licence limited to Philips
microcontrollers, so the USB Audio Class constants the descriptors need
are in a header of their own.

ALSA is now required on Linux.
